cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the FNC-1 task and the original project it re-implements."
title: "The Stance Desk: headline-article stance detection on FNC-1"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Akhil-428/The-Stance-Desk"
abstract: >-
  A leakage-controlled re-implementation of BERT-based stance detection on the
  Fake News Challenge (FNC-1) dataset, with bug-fixed baselines, the official
  FNC-1 score, and a Streamlit interface. Stance detection classifies how an
  article body relates to a headline (agree, disagree, discuss, unrelated); it
  does not verify whether a claim is true.
keywords:
  - stance detection
  - natural language processing
  - BERT
  - FNC-1
  - fake news
  - Streamlit
